# Personal site (joshmcvey.com)

Astro 6 static site on Cloudflare Pages. Audience: recruiters and hiring managers across three overlapping roles (consulting/trusted advisor, Build & Release / DevEx, staff SDET / platform engineering). One operator profile, not three pitches.

## Positioning (do not dilute)

- End-to-end shipper: Build & Release for two robot OSes and full Opentrons app suite, hands-on with the team (versions, tags, deployments).
- Full-stack on Opentrons AI and Protocol Library; owns auth across web products.
- Same week: standup, CTO architecture talk, Opentrons AI feature, API testing mentorship, release cut.
- Daily AI user: skills, rules, workflows for real dev practice.
- Strengths: process repair, data organization, relationships, creative framing, architecture. Not massive distributed-systems scale; yes pipeline repair, test infra, operational AI adoption.

## Required page sections (single home page)

1. Hero with specific positioning (no generic "full-stack engineer").
2. "What I'm good at" — three role types as facets of one profile.
3. Experience timeline from resume: 1–3 sentences per role; heavy Opentrons detail, older roles brief.
4. Selected projects (4–6 from github.com/y3rsh): title, description, language, link. Data from `src/data/github-projects.json` (committed cache). Refresh via `pnpm sync:github` (`scripts/sync-github-projects.mjs`).
5. "How I work with AI" — short, concrete; mention skills, rules, workflows.
6. Contact: LinkedIn, GitHub, email, resume PDF download (`public/resume.pdf`, no address, no phone).
7. Footer: current year.

## Machine-readable exports (keep in sync with resume facts)

- `/llms.txt`: llms.txt spec index pointing at resume and home.
- `/resume.txt` and `/resume.md`: full structured resume for AI agents (source: `src/content/resume-facts.ts`, formatted in `src/lib/resume-export.ts`).
- Update `resume-facts.ts` when experience or skills change; human copy in `site-copy.ts` should stay aligned.

## Copy voice (enforce on every edit)

First person, direct, specific. Rewrite any sentence that could live on a generic consulting site.

**Never use:** em dashes; leverage, robust, tapestry, landscape, delve, quietly, serves as, unlock, empower, seamless; "It's not X, it's Y"; "The X? A Y." fragments; anaphora or rule-of-three rhythm lists; imagine a world / think of it as / here's the kicker / let's unpack / let's dive in; transformative / revolutionary / redefining; vague attributions; bold-label bullet lists; gerund-fragment lists (Building X. Shipping Y.); In summary / At the end of the day; despite its challenges.

**Resume source:** `JoshMcveyResumeLinkedIn.pdf` for facts only; rephrase claims, do not paste LinkedIn summary wording.

## Tech conventions

- Site config: `src/site.ts`. Page copy: `src/content/`. GitHub types: `src/lib/github-projects.ts`.
- Keep components minimal; prefer Astro + CSS in `src/styles/global.css`.
- Node >=24, pnpm. Do not add phone or home address to the site.
